-- title:
--   Mod p Hecke eigenclass in parabolic cohomology of Γ₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$, an integer $n\ge 0$ and a set $S\subseteq\mathbb N$ containing every prime divisor of $N$, and let $\mathbb T=$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N (n+2) S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) be the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C} S_{n+2}(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to primes $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to primes $q\mid N$ with $q\notin S$ (the latter set being empty under the hypothesis on $S$). Let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$, $p\nmid N$ and $n<p$, let $Q$ be an arbitrary predicate on $\mathbb N$, let $a\colon\mathbb N\to\mathbb Z$ be an arbitrary function, and let $\mathfrak m\subset\mathbb T$ be a maximal ideal with $p\in\mathfrak m$ and $T_\ell-a(\ell)\in\mathfrak m$ for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$ and $Q(\ell)$, where $T_\ell=$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L77). Let $K$ be a field of characteristic $p$. Write $\rho$ for the representation of $\Gamma_0(N)$ on the degree-$n$ homogeneous part $\mathrm{BinaryForm}\,K\,n\subset K[X_0,X_1]$ obtained by restricting [`HeckeEis.binaryFormRepSL K n`](def/HeckeEis_BinaryFormRep.html#L61) (substitution of the matrix of $g$) along the inclusion $\Gamma_0(N)\hookrightarrow \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, and let $H^1_{\mathrm{par}}=$ [`HeckeEis.coeffH1par`](def/Gamma0CoeffCohomology.html#L100) $\rho$ be the quotient of the module of parabolic cocycles — functions $z\colon\Gamma_0(N)\to\mathrm{BinaryForm}\,K\,n$ with $z(gh)=z(g)+\rho(g)z(h)$ and $z(\gamma)\in\operatorname{im}(\rho(\gamma)-1)$ whenever $\operatorname{tr}(\gamma)^2=4$ — by those coboundaries that are parabolic cocycles. The assertion is that there exists a nonzero class $x\in H^1_{\mathrm{par}}$ such that for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$ and $Q(\ell)$ there is a $K$-linear endomorphism $T$ of $H^1_{\mathrm{par}}$ which is induced by the cochain-level operator [`HeckeEis.coeffHeckeFun N ℓ`](def/Gamma0CoeffCohomology.html#L129) with coefficient part [`HeckeEis.binaryFormAlphaAdj K n ℓ`](def/HeckeEis_BinaryFormRep.html#L82) (the substitution $F(X_0,X_1)\mapsto F(\ell X_0,X_1)$), in the sense that every parabolic cocycle $z$ admits a parabolic cocycle $w$ whose underlying function equals `coeffHeckeFun N ℓ` applied to $z$ and with $T[z]=[w]$, and which satisfies $T x=\overline{a(\ell)}\,x$ with $\overline{a(\ell)}$ the image of $a(\ell)$ in $K$. The existence of such an operator $T$ for each $\ell$ is part of the conclusion, and no uniqueness is claimed.
--
--   This is the passage from a maximal ideal of the Hecke algebra of $S_{n+2}(\Gamma_0(N))$ with residue characteristic $p$ to an actual mod $p$ Hecke eigenclass in the parabolic group cohomology $H^1_{\mathrm{par}}(\Gamma_0(N),\mathrm{Sym}^n K^2)$ — the Eichler–Shimura, Ash–Stevens form of the "going down" step, in the range $p$ odd, $p\nmid N$, $n<p$. It feeds the comparison of Hecke eigensystems in weights $2$ and $n+2$ used in the level-lowering part of the argument, being cited by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_mul_two_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra_two_or_succ`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_mul_two_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra_two_or_succ).
